{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012SZ2CgvQy5tt4hPPjDgAbP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NYWFMjhQ9jLkmgy8cdUP38","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Jyue/Documents/1-projects/Software Projects/pelangi-website\" && head -50 site/src/data/blog/posts.ts","description":"Read the beginning of posts.ts to see imports and type definitions"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8329,"cache_read_input_tokens":78297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8329},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a9745fe-924e-4c1e-a7db-632acf61f536","uuid":"e6f7cbb6-f790-4ff2-9596-71d0c79aab07"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NYWFMjhQ9jLkmgy8cdUP38","type":"tool_result","content":"export interface BlogPost {\r\n  slug: string;\r\n  title: string;\r\n  excerpt: string;\r\n  content: string; // HTML string\r\n  date: string; // YYYY-MM-DD\r\n  category: string;\r\n  author: string;\r\n  readTime: string;\r\n  readingTimeMinutes: number;\r\n  tags: string[];\r\n  featuredImage: string;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** Compute reading time from HTML content (200 wpm, minimum 1 min). */\r\nfunction computeReadingTime(html: string): number {\r\n  const text = html.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, \" \").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\r\n  const wordCount = text.split(\" \").filter(Boolean).length;\r\n  return Math.max(1, Math.ceil(wordCount / 200));\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** Converts a category label to a URL-safe slug. e.g. \"Food & Drink\" → \"food-drink\" */\r\nexport function categoryToSlug(category: string): string {\r\n  return category\r\n    .toLowerCase()\r\n    .replace(/[^a-z0-9\\s]/g, \"\")\r\n    .trim()\r\n    .replace(/\\s+/g, \"-\");\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** Converts a category slug back to a display label, or returns null if not found. */\r\nexport function slugToCategory(slug: string): string | null {\r\n  const found = blogPosts.find((p) => categoryToSlug(p.category) === slug);\r\n  return found ? found.category : null;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** All unique categories in the blog. */\r\nexport function getUniqueCategories(): string[] {\r\n  return [...new Set(blogPosts.map((p) => p.category))];\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst rawPosts: Omit<BlogPost, \"readingTimeMinutes\">[] = [\r\n  {\r\n    slug: \"ultimate-jb-food-guide-backpackers\",\r\n    title: \"The Ultimate Johor Bahru Food Guide for Backpackers (2026)\",\r\n    excerpt:\r\n      \"From RM5 hawker meals to legendary seafood spots — everything a budget traveller needs to eat their way through JB like a local.\",\r\n    date: \"2026-02-20\",\r\n    category: \"Food & Drink\",\r\n    author: \"Pelangi Team\",\n[rerun: b3]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a9745fe-924e-4c1e-a7db-632acf61f536","uuid":"1c913c49-7fb6-4cb0-9189-b71fe5a4e695","timestamp":"2026-04-13T20:07:56.764Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"export interface BlogPost {\r\n  slug: string;\r\n  title: string;\r\n  excerpt: string;\r\n  content: string; // HTML string\r\n  date: string; // YYYY-MM-DD\r\n  category: string;\r\n  author: string;\r\n  readTime: string;\r\n  readingTimeMinutes: number;\r\n  tags: string[];\r\n  featuredImage: string;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** Compute reading time from HTML content (200 wpm, minimum 1 min). */\r\nfunction computeReadingTime(html: string): number {\r\n  const text = html.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, \" \").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\r\n  const wordCount = text.split(\" \").filter(Boolean).length;\r\n  return Math.max(1, Math.ceil(wordCount / 200));\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** Converts a category label to a URL-safe slug. e.g. \"Food & Drink\" → \"food-drink\" */\r\nexport function categoryToSlug(category: string): string {\r\n  return category\r\n    .toLowerCase()\r\n    .replace(/[^a-z0-9\\s]/g, \"\")\r\n    .trim()\r\n    .replace(/\\s+/g, \"-\");\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** Converts a category slug back to a display label, or returns null if not found. */\r\nexport function slugToCategory(slug: string): string | null {\r\n  const found = blogPosts.find((p) => categoryToSlug(p.category) === slug);\r\n  return found ? found.category : null;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** All unique categories in the blog. */\r\nexport function getUniqueCategories(): string[] {\r\n  return [...new Set(blogPosts.map((p) => p.category))];\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst rawPosts: Omit<BlogPost, \"readingTimeMinutes\">[] = [\r\n  {\r\n    slug: \"ultimate-jb-food-guide-backpackers\",\r\n    title: \"The Ultimate Johor Bahru Food Guide for Backpackers (2026)\",\r\n    excerpt:\r\n      \"From RM5 hawker meals to legendary seafood spots — everything a budget traveller needs to eat their way through JB like a local.\",\r\n    date: \"2026-02-20\",\r\n    category: \"Food & Drink\",\r\n    author: \"Pelangi Team\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01RqLwd8zpjLJ1ytz5DLVdrK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Now I have the complete picture. I need to:\n\n1. Create a new blog post object for US-244 with:\n   - slug: 'jb-singapore-commuter-guide-2026'\n   - title: Something appropriate\n   - excerpt: A brief summary\n   - content: HTML with bus services list and monthly cost breakdown\n   - date: '2026-04-14'\n   - category: 'Career & Work'\n   - author: 'Pelangi Team'\n   - readTime: '8 min read' (but I'll make sure the content is correct length)\n   - tags: relevant tags\n   - featuredImage: an appropriate image\n   \n2. Make sure to:\n   - Keep HTML under 8000 characters\n   - Include bus service list with prices\n   - Include monthly cost breakdown table\n   - Include internal links to /getting-here and /rooms\n   - Add it to the rawPosts array before the last closing bracket\n\nLet me create the plan:","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":980,"cache_read_input_tokens":86626,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":980},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a9745fe-924e-4c1e-a7db-632acf61f536","uuid":"1ba95272-b31e-4443-905e-cf94ae89522f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01RqLwd8zpjLJ1ytz5DLVdrK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Current State\nThe blog post system is a static TypeScript array (`rawPosts`) in `site/src/data/blog/posts.ts`. Each post has metadata (slug, title, excerpt, date, category, author, readTime, tags, featuredImage) and HTML content embedded as a template literal. The previous post (US-243) follows this exact structure.\n\n## Problem Identified\nNeed to create a new blog post for US-244 about living in Johor Bahru while working in Singapore. The post must include:\n- Slug: 'jb-singapore-commuter-guide-2026'\n- Category: 'Career & Work' \n- HTML list of bus services with prices\n- Monthly cost breakdown table\n- Internal links to /getting-here and /rooms\n- readTime: '8 min read', date: '2026-04-14'\n- HTML content under 8000 characters\n\n## Planned Changes\n- Add new blog post object to `rawPosts` array in `site/src/data/blog/posts.ts`\n- Include bus service options (Causeway Link/SBS) with prices\n- Include monthly cost breakdown comparing JB vs Singapore\n- Add internal links to /getting-here and /rooms\n- Ensure HTML stays under 8000 characters\n- Run `npm run build` to verify\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\"site/src/data/blog/posts.ts\"],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 120\n}\n</plan>\n\nNow implementing the blog post:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":980,"cache_read_input_tokens":86626,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":980},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a9745fe-924e-4c1e-a7db-632acf61f536","uuid":"1d013b8a-6991-41d8-b854-b99ef9c9a749"}
